        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Vatra',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Vatra ('Fire') is a card-passing party game for 3-13 players. Each player gets 4 cards (one rank per player). Pass cards to collect four-of-a-kind. First to four-of-a-kind calls 'Vatra!' Loser (last without) gets punishment: winner shuffles deck, loser names a card, cards flipped â€” each suit before that card = specific physical penalty.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Vatra (Fire) and Magarac (Jackass) are versions of Pig without a stock played in Bosnia and Herzegovina. They belong to the card-passing family; players pass cards in turn rather than simultaneously like basic Pig. Vatra uses physical punishment and is traditionally played by young boys.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two or more players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Use 4 cards per player (one complete rank each). Extra deck for punishment.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '4 cards each (one rank per player in deck).',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
